<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3418] TcpDiscoverySpi: lots of duplicated node failed messages</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3418</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently in TcpDiscoverySpi there is safety check called when discovery worker thread is idle: if node from &apos;failed list&apos; still in ring then send &apos;node failed&apos; message for such node (&apos;ServerImpl.checkFailedNodesList&apos;). This can lead to lots of duplicated unnecessary messages. &lt;br/&gt;
This check should be changed: need send event only once and only in case when node which marked node as failed left cluster.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
